  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the first $n$ terms of the series $1^2+2 \\cdot 2^2+3^2+2 \\cdot 4^2+5^2+2 \\cdot 6^2+\\ldots$ is $\\frac{n(n+1)^2}{2}$ when $n$ is even. When $n$ is odd the sum is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EEv1J",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 n(n+1)}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FgeTx",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{n}^2(\\mathrm{n}+1)}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mgdAd",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{n(n+1)^2}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jrPWV",
      "text": "\n$\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}+1)}{2}\\right]^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If $n$ is odd then $(n-1)$ is even $\\Rightarrow$ sum of odd terms $=\\frac{(n-1) n^2}{2}+n^2=\\frac{n^2(n+1)}{2}$.",
    "image": null
  },
